{"version":"10.0","level":"4","subject":"en","questions":[{"id":"EN-4-05269","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Choose the sentence with correct punctuation.","correct":"My name is Hana.","answers":["none","both","My name is Hana.","my name is Hana"],"explanation":"A sentence starts with a capital letter and ends with punctuation.","concept":"sentence-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05118","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"I have ___ apple.","correct":"an","answers":["the","some","a","an"],"explanation":"Use “an” before a word that begins with a vowel sound.","concept":"grammar-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05033","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “happy” is…","correct":"sad","answers":["young","weak","late","sad"],"explanation":"“sad” is the opposite of “happy”.","concept":"ant-happy","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05048","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “strong” is…","correct":"weak","answers":["far","weak","heavy","strong"],"explanation":"“weak” is the opposite of “strong”.","concept":"ant-strong","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05015","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “hot” is…","correct":"cold","answers":["young","big","cold","dirty"],"explanation":"“cold” is the opposite of “hot”.","concept":"ant-hot","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05312","topic":"Comprehension","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Read: “Adam found a wallet and gave it to his teacher.”\n\nWhat quality did Adam show?","correct":"Honesty.","answers":["Laziness.","Honesty.","Anger.","Carelessness."],"explanation":"Returning a lost wallet shows honesty.","concept":"comp-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05208","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Ali walks ___ school.","correct":"to","answers":["in","to","from","on"],"explanation":"“to” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05219","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The ball is ___ the two chairs.","correct":"between","answers":["under","from","between","into"],"explanation":"“between” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05192","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The book is ___ the table.","correct":"on","answers":["between","on","from","at"],"explanation":"“on” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05140","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"My sister and I ___ pupils.","correct":"are","answers":["am","is","are","was"],"explanation":"A compound plural subject takes “are”.","concept":"grammar-5","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05071","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Which word means a baby cat?","correct":"kitten","answers":["chick","puppy","calf","kitten"],"explanation":"The correct word is “kitten”.","concept":"vocab-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05177","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Last night, they ___ a movie.","correct":"watched","answers":["watching","watched","watch","watches"],"explanation":"“Last night” signals past tense.","concept":"tense-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05156","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Every morning, Siti ___ milk.","correct":"drinks","answers":["drank","drinking","drinks","drink"],"explanation":"A repeated daily action uses the simple present: “drinks”.","concept":"tense-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05169","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Tomorrow, we ___ visit the museum.","correct":"will","answers":["has","did","was","will"],"explanation":"“Tomorrow” indicates future time; “will” is appropriate.","concept":"tense-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05107","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"They ___ happy.","correct":"are","answers":["be","am","is","are"],"explanation":"The plural subject “they” takes “are”.","concept":"grammar-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05239","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Choose the correct sentence.","correct":"She likes reading books.","answers":["Likes she reading books.","She likes reading books.","She like reading books.","She books likes reading."],"explanation":"The subject and verb agree, and the word order is correct.","concept":"sentence-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05309","topic":"Comprehension","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Read: “The pupils planted five trees behind the school. They water the trees every afternoon.”\n\nWhere did the pupils plant the trees?","correct":"Behind the school.","answers":["In the classroom.","Behind the school.","Beside a hospital.","At the market."],"explanation":"The location is stated directly in the passage.","concept":"comp-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05187","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Now, the children are ___ in the park.","correct":"playing","answers":["plays","played","play","playing"],"explanation":"After “are”, use the -ing form for an action happening now.","concept":"tense-4","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05223","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The picture is ___ the wall.","correct":"on","answers":["under","to","on","from"],"explanation":"“on” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-4","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05053","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “near” is…","correct":"far","answers":["cold","light","hot","far"],"explanation":"“far” is the opposite of “near”.","concept":"ant-near","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05035","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “early” is…","correct":"late","answers":["early","late","big","near"],"explanation":"“late” is the opposite of “early”.","concept":"ant-early","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05025","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “fast” is…","correct":"slow","answers":["slow","cold","early","big"],"explanation":"“slow” is the opposite of “fast”.","concept":"ant-fast","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05199","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The cat is ___ the box.","correct":"in","answers":["with","to","from","in"],"explanation":"“in” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05154","topic":"Tenses","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Yesterday, Amir ___ football.","correct":"played","answers":["play","played","playing","plays"],"explanation":"“Yesterday” signals past tense, so use “played”.","concept":"tense-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05246","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Choose the correct sentence.","correct":"We are going to the market.","answers":["We going are the market.","Are we going market the.","We are going to the market.","We is going market."],"explanation":"This sentence has correct subject-verb agreement and word order.","concept":"sentence-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05278","topic":"Comprehension","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Read: “Ben has a red bicycle. He rides it to the park every Sunday.”\n\nWhat colour is Ben’s bicycle?","correct":"red","answers":["blue","yellow","red","green"],"explanation":"The passage says the bicycle is red.","concept":"comp-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05066","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Which word means a place where we borrow books?","correct":"library","answers":["garage","kitchen","clinic","library"],"explanation":"The correct word is “library”.","concept":"vocab-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05085","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Which word means a place where doctors treat patients?","correct":"hospital","answers":["stadium","hospital","market","library"],"explanation":"The correct word is “hospital”.","concept":"vocab-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05263","topic":"Sentence","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Choose the correct question.","correct":"Where are you going?","answers":["Where are you going?","Where you are going.","Going where you are?","Where is you going?"],"explanation":"Questions with “you” use “are” before the subject.","concept":"sentence-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05232","topic":"Prepositions","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The shoes are ___ the bed.","correct":"under","answers":["to","under","between","from"],"explanation":"“under” fits the location or direction in this sentence.","concept":"prep-5","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05058","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “young” is…","correct":"old","answers":["weak","small","slow","old"],"explanation":"“old” is the opposite of “young”.","concept":"ant-young","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05061","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “light” is…","correct":"heavy","answers":["hot","heavy","light","cold"],"explanation":"“heavy” is the opposite of “light”.","concept":"ant-light","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05096","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Which word means an animal that gives us milk?","correct":"cow","answers":["ant","shark","eagle","cow"],"explanation":"The correct word is “cow”.","concept":"vocab-4","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05127","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"These ___ my books.","correct":"are","answers":["be","am","are","is"],"explanation":"“These” is plural, so use “are”.","concept":"grammar-3","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05039","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “clean” is…","correct":"dirty","answers":["near","late","heavy","dirty"],"explanation":"“dirty” is the opposite of “clean”.","concept":"ant-clean","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05296","topic":"Comprehension","difficulty":"sederhana","question":"Read: “Maya wakes up at seven o’clock. She eats breakfast before going to school.”\n\nWhat does Maya do before school?","correct":"She eats breakfast.","answers":["She eats breakfast.","She watches a movie.","She goes swimming.","She goes to bed."],"explanation":"The passage states that Maya eats breakfast before school.","concept":"comp-1","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05136","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"He ___ a blue bicycle.","correct":"has","answers":["is","are","has","have"],"explanation":"Use “has” with he/she/it in the simple present.","concept":"grammar-4","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05101","topic":"Grammar","difficulty":"mudah","question":"She ___ to school every day.","correct":"goes","answers":["gone","goes","going","go"],"explanation":"With “she” in the simple present, use “goes”.","concept":"grammar-0","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05081","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"Which word means a person who teaches pupils?","correct":"teacher","answers":["farmer","pilot","teacher","chef"],"explanation":"The correct word is “teacher”.","concept":"vocab-2","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"},{"id":"EN-4-05020","topic":"Vocabulary","difficulty":"mudah","question":"The opposite of “big” is…","correct":"small","answers":["young","old","light","small"],"explanation":"“small” is the opposite of “big”.","concept":"ant-big","qa":"v10-reviewed","source":"LatihKu Original","alignment":"KPM-aligned","itemType":"mcq"}]}